   - If `arr2[j]` comes before `arr1[i]`, move `j` to the next index such that `j < arr2.length() && arr2[j] >= arr1[i]`. Similarly, this ensures that we don't recheck the same element when searching for `i`th's position in `arr2`.
3. After the loop terminates, check if `count > 0`. If so, return an array containing all matched elements with their count as the frequency. Else, return an empty or null array.

